R. UABOI OVBIAGELE V. MRS. JULIET OVBIAGELE ARCHIVES July 2026 (28) June 2026 (22) May 2026 (2) April 2026 (4) March 2026 (5) February 2026 (5) January 2026 (2) December 2025 (1) October 2025 (4) September 2025 (1) July 2025 (3) June 2025 (12) May 2025 (10) April 2025 (3) March 2025 (2) February 2025 (4) January 2025 (1) December 2024 (2) November 2024 (202) October 2024 (84) September 2024 (169) August 2024 (2) July 2024 (2) June 2024 (452) May 2024 (17) April 2024 (2) March 2024 (3) January 2024 (3) November 2023 (1) October 2023 (3) June 2023 (1) May 2023 (1) April 2023 (2) March 2023 (1) January 2023 (3) December 2022 (1) November 2022 (1) October 2022 (3) July 2022 (4) June 2022 (1) May 2022 (3) April 2022 (2) March 2022 (1) January 2022 (1) November 2021 (2) October 2021 (1) September 2021 (1) July 2021 (1) June 2021 (2) CALENDAR July 2026 M T W T F S S 12345 6789101112 13141516171819 20212223242526 2728293031 \u00ab Jun Scroll to Top", "content_hash": "49ca6cf3eabb70001ac1ac288ea4b4780a398a0a5776b50da105ec12cfa70b2d", "domain": "nigerianlawguru.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:26:55.219715+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1794", "title": "Ex-Delta Governor, Uduaghan is dead", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/news-former-delta-governor-uduaghan-is-dead/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/news-former-delta-governor-uduaghan-is-dead/", "text": "[News](https://dailypost.ng/hot-news/)Ex-Delta Governor, Uduaghan is deadPublished on October 19, 2026By [Matthew Omonigho](https://dailypost.ng/author/matthew-omonigho/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/news-former-delta-governor-uduaghan-is-dead/comments/)A former Governor of Delta State, Dr. Emmanuel Uduaghan is dead.He died after a brief illness at the age of 71.The Uduaghan family announced his death in a statement signed by Toju Andre Uduaghan, on Monday.The statement, titled, 'ANNOUNCEMENT OF THE PASSING OF HIS EXCELLENCY, DR. CHIEF EMMANUEL EWETA UDUAGHAN', read:Recommended[Bauchi NDC guber candidate resigns from party](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-ndc-guber-candidate-dumps-party/)['Congratulations to Tinubu' - Atiku\u2019s aide mocks President over UN budget](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/congratulations-to-tinubu-atikus-aide-mocks-president-over-un-budget/)[Tinubu releases N4bn for payment of 600 ex-Nigeria Airways workers](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/tinubu-releases-n4bn-severance-pay-for-600-ex-nigeria-airways-workers-2/)\"It is with hearts weighed down by immeasurable grief and profound sorrow that we announce the passing to glory of our beloved Father, Brother, Uncle, and Patriarch, His Excellency, Dr. Chief Emmanuel Eweta Uduaghan, former Governor of Delta State, who departed this world on the morning of 19th October 2026.\"His passing has left us devastated. Words can hardly express the depth of our sorrow at the loss of a man who meant so much to our family and whose life and service touched countless others across Delta State and Nigeria.\"He was a source of strength, a father figure, a beloved brother and uncle, and a respected elder. We will deeply miss his presence and forever cherish the memories and legacy he leaves behind.\"He served as Commissioner for Health from 1999 to 2003, Secretary to the Delta State Government from 2003 to 2007, and Governor of Delta State from 2007 to 2015. Throughout his years in public service, he demonstrated a commitment to the human and infrastructural development of Delta State.\"His passing is a profound loss to our family, the people of Delta State, and Nigeria at large. We are grateful to Almighty God for his life, his service, and the legacy he leaves behind.\"We pray that Almighty God, in His infinite mercy, will grant his soul eternal rest and comfort our family, friends, associates, former colleagues, and all who mourn this painful loss.\"Rest well, our beloved Father, Brother, and Uncle. Your memory will forever remain in our hearts, and your legacy will endure in the lives of those you touched.\"May your gentle soul rest in perfect peace. Amen.\"Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=Ex-Delta%20Governor%2C%20Uduaghan%20is%20dead%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F19%2Fnews-former-delta-governor-uduaghan-is-dead%2F) FacebookYou may like[Dele Giwa: IPC demands justice 40 years after assassination](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/dele-giwa-ipc-demands-justice-forty-years-after-assassination/)[NMA Chairman laments challenges faced by doctors in Kaduna](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/nma-chairman-laments-on-challenges-face-by-doctors-in-kaduna/)[Borno: Scrap dealers challenge Zulum over alleged N3bn cable theft](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/borno-scrap-dealers-challenge-zulum-over-alleged-n3bn-cable-theft/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/news-former-delta-governor-uduaghan-is-dead/comments/)", "content_hash": "4fb98b4a4ca84bac5063dfff50aecd2d1c8d32215820344ffa0b937941192263", "domain": "dailypost.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:26:55.630145+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1795", "title": "Attempt", "url": "https://nigerianlawguru.com/caselaw_digest/attempt-2/", "final_url": "https://nigerianlawguru.com/caselaw_digest/attempt-2/", "text": "Attempt Skip to content email: info@nigerianlawguru.cominfo@nigerianlawguru.com Phone: +2347066957900+2347066957900 Contact Us: Benin City, Nigeria Open Menu Home Our Team Articles Arbitration Commercial Law Company Law Constitutional Law Criminal Law and Procedure Customary Law and Procedure Family Law Environmental Law General Human Rights Law Insurance Intellectual Property Law International Law Jurisprudence Labour Law Maritime Law Oil and Gas Practice and Procedure Revenue Law Torts HOW TO TENDER AND PLAY VIDEO EVIDENCE IN COURT Caselaw Digest Legislations Constitutions of Nations Laws of the Federation of Nigeria Oil and Gas Legislations Rules Statutes Judgments Chieftaincy Matters Commercial Law Constitutional Law Criminal Law Customary Law Election 