pam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "3bc49278e3f2022444a1dd86e17f68d7e0f92c888749ca8d2f021b4b45ce10ba", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:42.562754+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1851", "title": "Press Release: DMO Lists N47.335 Billion Series III Green Bond on NGX and FMDQ Exchanges - Debt Management Office Nigeria", "url": "https://dmo.gov.ng/press-release-dmo-lists-n47-335-billion-series-iii-green-bond-on-ngx-and-fmdq-exchanges", "final_url": "https://dmo.gov.ng/press-release-dmo-lists-n47-335-billion-series-iii-green-bond-on-ngx-and-fmdq-exchanges", "text": "Press Release: DMO Lists N47.335 Billion Series III Green Bond on NGX and FMDQ Exchanges - Debt Management Office Nigeria Debt Management Office Nigeria HomeSitemapJoin UsFeedback Search ... MENU \u00d7 HomeAbout US About DMODepartmentsManagement TeamDebt ProfileDomestic DebtsDebt StockDebt ServiceExternal DebtsDebt StockDebt ServiceSub-National DebtsTotal Public DebtsContingent LiabilitiesBonds FGN BondsEurobonds TradingBonds Auction ResultsFGN Bond UpdatesNigerian Treasury BillsPrimary Dealer Market MakersBonds Issuance CalendarBonds Offer CircularSavings BondSovereign SukukGreen Bond Promissory NotesDomestic FGN US Dollar Bond News & EventsCirculars & ReleasesDMO In The NewsTendersPublicationsReportsDMO Annual Report & Statement of AccountsDebt Sustainability AnalysisOther PublicationsBorrowing GuidelinesDebt Management StrategyDMO Client Service Charter DMO Strategic PlanDMO Establishment ActNational Debt Management FrameworkSub-national Debt ManagementNigeria's Debt ReliefDMO's Ease of Doing Business GuideNigeria Public Debt Statistical BulletinContact Us Home About US About DMO Departments Management Team Debt Profile Domestic Debts Debt Stock Debt Service External Debts Debt Stock Debt Service Sub-National Debts Total Public Debts Contingent Liabilities Bonds FGN Bonds Eurobonds Trading Bonds Auction Results FGN Bond Updates Nigerian Treasury Bills Primary Dealer Market Makers Bonds Issuance Calendar Bonds Offer Circular Savings Bond Sovereign Sukuk Green Bond Promissory Notes Domestic FGN US Dollar Bond News & Events Circulars & Releases DMO In The News Tenders Publications Reports DMO Annual Report & Statement of Accounts Debt Sustainability Analysis Other Publications Borrowing Guidelines Debt Management Strategy DMO Client Service Charter DMO Strategic Plan DMO Establishment Act National Debt Management Framework Sub-national Debt Management Nigeria's Debt Relief DMO's Ease of Doing Business Guide Nigeria Public Debt Statistical Bulletin Contact Us LATEST : DG DMO, Patience Oniha, at the 2026 IMF Spring Meetings at Washington D.C., U.S.A. - 27 April 2026 DG DMO, Patience Oniha, at the 2026 IMF Spring Meetings at Washington D.C., U.S.A. - 27 April 2026 DG DMO, Patience Oniha, at the Nigeria\u2019s Reform Scorecard (2023 - 2026) Press Conference on August 19, 2026 - 24 August 2026 DMO receives two Awards at the EMEA Finance Achievement Awards 2025 - 16 June 2026 DMO wins two prestigious awards at the Global Banking Markets Africa Awards 2026 - 10 April 2026 Press Release: DMO Lists N47.335 Billion Series III Green Bond on NGX and FMDQ Exchanges Wednesday, 13 May 2026 08:03 Press Release: DMO Lists N47.335 Billion Series III Green Bond on NGX and FMDQ Exchanges font size decrease font size increase font size Print Email DEBT MANAGEMENT OFFICE NIGERIA PRESS RELEASE DMO LISTS N47.335 BILLION SERIES III GREEN BOND ON NGX AND FMDQ EXCHANGES The Debt Management Office (DMO) is pleased to announce the Listing of the 18.95% \u20a647.355 Billion Series III Sovereign Green Bond due June 2030 on the Nigerian Exchange Limited and FMDQ Securities Exchange Limited on May 13, 2026. The Green Bond, which is the third to be issued by the DMO on behalf of the Federal Government of Nigeria, is an attestation to the DMO\u2019s commitment to providing funds needed to finance green projects that support Nigeria\u2019s commitment towards achieving a low-carbon and climate-resilient society. In addition, through the issuance of Green Bonds, the DMO is increasing visibility for climate-focused financial instruments in the domestic market, while also providing ethical investors with securities that meet their investment preferences. The Listing of the Green Bond is to provide liquidity to investors and achieve price transparency. The DMO acknowledges the collaboration of the Transaction Parties to the issuance of the Green Bond, namely, the Issuing Houses and Bookrunners - Chapel Hill Denham and Stanbic IBTC Capital Limited and the Legal Adviser - S.P.A. Ajibade and Co., as well as other market stakeholders. The DMO reiterates its commitments to providing a wide range of securities to meet the needs of diverse investors while also, deepening the domestic bond market. DEBT MANAGEMENT OFFICE The Presidency NDIC Building (First Floor), Plot 447/448 Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, P.M.B. 532, Garki, Abuja Tel: +234 \u2013 8110000881-3 Website: http://www.dmo.gov.ng, Email: This email address is being protected from spambots. You need JavaScript enabled to view it. May 13, 2026 Tweet Published in DMO In The News More in this category: \u00ab DG DMO, Patience Oniha, at the 2026 IMF Spring Meetings at Washington D.C., U.S.A. DMO receives two Awards at the EMEA Finance Achievement Awards 2025 \u00bb back to top Latest Publications. pdf Nigeria's Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yields as at Wednesday, October 7, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 08 October 2026 spreadsheet Nigeria's Daily Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yeilds from October 07, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 08 October 2026 pdf Nigeria's Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yields as at Tuesday, October 6, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 07 October 2026 spreadsheet Nigeria's Daily Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yeilds from October 06, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 07 October 2026 pdf Nigeria's Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yields as at Monday, October 5, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 06 October 2026 spreadsheet Nigeria's Daily Eurobonds Closing Prices and Yeilds from October 05, 2026 New Popular In Eurobonds Trading 06 October 2026 pdf FGN Savings Bond Offer for Subscription October, 2026 New Popular In Savings Bond 05 October 2026 DMO In The News DG DMO, Patience Oniha, at the Nigeria\u2019s Reform Scorecard (2023 - 2026) Press Conference on August 19, 2026 24/08/2026 / DMO In The News Read more Subscribe to Publications Copyright \u00a9 2026 Debt Management Office Nigeria. All Rights Reserved. Data Protection Privacy NoticeArchive Staff Login", "content_hash": "af851162e512977556b5bcb21ac54410c103b2650c2771d361942111d989516c", "domain": "dmo.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:42.787615+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1852", "title": "Electrotechnical", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/technical-committees/electrotechnical/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/technical-committees/electrotechnical/", "text": "Electrotechnical \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Cha