l Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2026 - 2028 MTEF & FSP Home 2026 - 2028 MTEF & FSP 2026 - 2028 MTEF & FSP Published on 17 December 2025 File Name: 2026 - 2028 MTEF&FSP - Post FEC.pdf File Size: 2.83 MB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 5966 Hits Created Date: 12-17-2025 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "4b5c668f37fd059da555a34b27711649a647b9c3ef87dfa816103eef6bfd190d", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:58.834200+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1862", "title": "NRCAP", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/technical-committees/services/nrcap/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/technical-committees/services/nrcap/", "text": "NRCAP \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Charges SMEs Desk Standards PAM Inspectorate & Compliance NRCAP Resources Management Systems Certification SON-MSC ISO Audit Process Flowchart Impartiality Policy Client Database Service Charge Policies Turn Around Time Suspension, Refusal, Cancellation, Scope Reduction and Expansion Policy Policy on the Use of Management Systems Certification Mark and Logo Service Process Flow Chart Application Form Management Systems Certification Contract Terms and Conditions with Client Complaint & Appeals Procedure Complaints Form Enquiry Training Training Services Training Services 2026 Training Calendar Ports & Border Port & Border: Field Inspection Process & Charges Port & Border Service Process Flow Chart Library Library Service Process Flow Chart Media Center News & Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng search Menu NRCAP BRIEF ON NATIONAL REGISTER FOR CONFORMITY ASSESMENT PRACTITIONERS \u2013 NRCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria demonstrates unwavering resolve to sanitise the conformity Assessment practice in Nigeria in line with the provisions of the law (Part III, section 5 of the SON ACT No. 14 of 2015 \u201cto establish Registration and Regulation for National Standards, Standard Marks, Certification Systems and Licenses\u201d via the operation of the NRCAP scheme in order to establish a directory of verified and registered Conformity Assessment Practitioners in Nigeria for all Laboratories, Management system Auditors, Trainers, Inspectors, Consultants, Inspection and Certification bodies). According to, ISO/IEC 17000:2004, Conformity assessment\u2014Vocabulary and general principles, defines conformity assessment as \u201cdemonstration that specified requirements relating to a product, process, system, person or body are fulfilled. Conformity assessment services are usually performed by organizations specializing in one or other activities, of which the main ones are described below: Testing \u2013 A product is tested against a specific set of criteria, such as performance or safety. Testing is the most common form of conformity assessment. Testing also provides the basis for other types of conformity assessment such as inspection and product certification. Inspection \u2013 Inspection bodies play an essential role in cross-border trade. They act on behalf of governments and business partners (importers and exporters) by inspecting imported goods and materials. They are responsible for examining a huge range of products, materials, installations, plants, processes, work procedures and services, in the private as well as the public sector, and report on such parameters as quality, fitness for use and continuing safety in operation. The overall aim is to reduce risk to the buyer, owner, user or consumer of the item being inspected. Government and business often use their services to inspect imported goods and materials. Certification \u2013 Certification is when a certification body gives written assurance that a product, service, process, personnel, organization or management system conforms to specific requirements. The most well-known examples are the certification of quality management systems and environmental management systems as conforming, respectively, to the ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 standards. Newer management standards that also allow for certification address food safety (ISO 22000), energy management (ISO 50001) occupational safety and health while at work (1SO 45001) and information security (ISO/IEC 27001). The scope of coverage for registration to the NRCAP Scheme include: Management system consultants Management system Training service Providers Laboratory/Calibration Testing Service Providers Inspections Bodies Certification Bodies Personnel Category: Auditors, Inspectors etc. BRIEF ON NATIONAL REGISTER FOR CONFORMITY ASSESMENT PRACTITIONERS \u2013 NRCAP FLOWCHART FOR REGISTRATION TO THE SCHEME ENQUIRY (ololade.ayoola@son.gov.ng, Theophilus.edi@son.gov.ng, Nkechi.ohaemesi@son.gov.ng, 08066089166, 08032566738, 08032701976) APPLICATION FORM SUBMISION OF NECESSARY DOCUMENTATION EVALUATION ADVICE TO MAKE RELEVANT PAYMENT CONFIRMATION OF PAYMENT REVIEW OF RECOMMENDATION FOR REGISTRATION/USE OF LOGO COMMUNICATION OF MANAGEMENT DECISION S/N NAME & ADDRESS OF COMPANY COMFORMITY NUMBER SERVICES E-MAIL ADDRESS 1 Guidepilots Solutions Limited,43b Emina Crescent, Off Toyin Street, Ikeja \u2013Lagos SON-NR-MC-0004 MANAGEMENT SYSTEM CONSULTANT -ISO-9001:2015 info@guidepilotssolutions.com 2 Royal Certification Limited, Suite 2, Musa Gwadabe, ksip Plaza -15 Murtala Muhammed Way, Nasarawa GRA -Kano SON-NR-MC-0001 SON-NR-MC-0002 MANAGEMENT SYSTEM CONSULTANT -ISO-9001:2015 & ISO-14001:2015 yerimaabdul@hotmail.com 3 Noscow Instrument Technology Limited, 155, Lagos Abeokuta Express, Beside Access Bank, Iyana \u2013 Ipaja, Lagos SON-NR-L-00001 MOBILE CALIBRATION LABORATORY SERVICE PROVIDER noscowinstrument@gmail.com 4 Top Three Concept Nigeria Limited, Bola Arowol