t-certification/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/international-product-certification/", "text": "International Product Certification \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Charges SMEs Desk Standards PAM Inspectorate & Compliance NRCAP Resources Management Systems Certification SON-MSC ISO Audit Process Flowchart Impartiality Policy Client Database Service Charge Policies Turn Around Time Suspension, Refusal, Cancellation, Scope Reduction and Expansion Policy Policy on the Use of Management Systems Certification Mark and Logo Service Process Flow Chart Application Form Management Systems Certification Contract Terms and Conditions with Client Complaint & Appeals Procedure Complaints Form Enquiry Training Training Services Training Services 2026 Training Calendar Ports & Border Port & Border: Field Inspection Process & Charges Port & Border Service Process Flow Chart Library Library Service Process Flow Chart Media Center News & Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng search Menu International Product Certification INTERNATIONAL PRODUCT CERTTIFICATION DEPARTMENT(IPCD) Introduction The International Product Certification Department (IPCD) is a specialized department of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), established through the restructuring of the former Product Certification Department to enhance efficiency, strengthen international operations, and align with global best practices in conformity assessment. The Department is responsible for managing all offshore conformity assessment and certification activities relating to imported products destined for the Nigerian market, with a focus on ensuring compliance with Nigerian Industrial Standards (NIS) and applicable technical regulations. Mandate of IPCD The mandate of the department is derived from Section (5) of the SON Act No. 14 of 2015 stipulates that SON shall Establish an Import and Export Product Surveillance, Certification and Conformity Assessment Scheme. Undertake registration of all manufactured products distributed, marketed, and consumed throughout Nigeria. Strategic Objectives The IPCD is guided by the following strategic objectives: Enhance efficiency and transparency in certification of imported products Strengthen risk-based conformity assessment systems Improve revenue generation and accountability Support Nigeria\u2019s participation in WTO TBT, AfCFTA, and other trade agreements Protect consumers and the environment from unsafe products INTERNATION PRODUCT CERTIFICATION SCHEMES There are Four (4) main product certification schemes operated by the Organisation through the International Product Certification Department: SON Conformity Assessment Programme(SONCAP) Product Registration SON Mandatory Energy Labelling Scheme (SONMELS) The SON\u2013NADDC Vehicle Conformity Assessment Programme (VehCAP) FUNCTIONAL STRUCTURE The International Product Certification Department comprises of the Office of the Director and four Divisions. SONCAP Division Product Registration Division SON Mandatory Energy Labelling Scheme (SONMELS) Division The SON-NADDC Vehicle Conformity Assessment Programme STANDARDS ORGANISATION OF NIGERIA CONFORMITY ASSESSMENT PROGRAMME (SONCAP) SONCAPSONCAP FLOW PROCESSSONCAP SERVICE CHARGE The SONCAP Division is charged with the surveillance and monitoring of the conformance of imported product to SON regulatory requirements as mandated by the SON Act No. 14 of 2015. The Division is responsible for the management of the utilization of the Product Certificates and Shipment Certificates, issued by the IAFs, for the processing of CBN FormM and the NCS PAAR respectively, to serve as precursor to the actual cargo clearance process at the ports. The Division is also responsible for managing the process for the issuance of SONCAP Import Permit to bonafide manufacturers and to some importers of some selected non-commercial articles. The objectives of the programme include but are not limited to the following: Ensure that regulated products comply with the NIS or approved standards prior to export to Nigeria Provide a level playing field in terms of quality for both regulated and locally manufactured products in order to prevent unfair competition Prevent the dumping of substandard goods into the Nigeria market and as a result preventing economic loss to the importer and the nation at large Impede loss of lives and property including foreign exchange bearing in mind that the exporting country/Exporter have been paid for the goods shipped into Nigeria Forestall any adverse reaction (such as environmental pollution occasioned by destruction of substandard products) by regulatory Agencies on arrival of such goods in Nigeria Facilitate trade through fast track clearance of goods at the ports Encourage genuine investors and investments in Nigeria Promote made in Nigeria products Conserve foreign exchange APPLY HERE/ MORE ABOUT SONCAP SON MANDATORY ENERGY LABELLING SCHEME (SONMELs) SONMELs establishes conformity assessment framework for to support implementation of mandatory energy performance standards and energy labeling requirements for selected appliances pursuance to section 5(1)(h) of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria Act, 2015. This is to ensure that energy-consuming appliances placed on the Nigerian market meet prescribed Minimum Energy Performance Standards (MEPS) and carry the appropriate energy label The objectives of the Division are as follows: Empower consumers with transparent energy efficiency information Promote energy conservation and reduce electricity consumption to support national climate commitments Reduce household electricity costs and the demand on national grid; Prevent dumping of inefficient appliances in the Nigerian market; Incentivize manufacturers to invest in energy-efficient technologies to improve market access for made in Nigeria appliances in other countries. APPLY HERE/ MORE ABOUT SONMELs PRODUCT REGISTRATION DIVISION (PIS) PRODUCT REGISTRATION DIVISIONFLOW PROCESSSERVICE CHARGE The Product Registration Division is responsible for the registration and maintenance of a database of all imported SON regulated products sold in Nigeria, as well as their importer and distributor details nationwide. The objectives of the Division are as follows: To Ensure that every product imported into Nigeria is registered and issued a number and logo before they are sold in the Nigeria markets. To ensure that only good quality products are sold in the Nigerian markets. To ensure traceability of all products. To ensure that Nigeria is not a dumping ground for substandard products.. To protect the consumers and ensure that they get value for their money. SON VEHICLE CONFORMITY ASSESSMENT PROGRAMME (VehCAP) Coming soon\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 The Standards Organisation of Nigeria 52, Lome Crescent, Zone 7, Wuse, Abuja, FCT. Technical Committees Food & Agriculture Textile and Leather Chemical Technology Mechanical Electrotechnical Civil Services Trade Affairs Quick LinksManagement System Certification Meet The Management Team MANCAP International Product Certification SONCAP Privacy Policy Training Services LPG Follow SON Online facebook instagram twitter linkedin youtube \u00a9 2026 Standards Organisation of Nigeria. Site Map Close Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Charges SMEs Desk Standards PAM Inspectorate & Compliance NRCAP Resources Management Systems Certification SON-MSC ISO Audit Process Flowchart Impartiality Policy Client Database Service Charge Policies Turn Around Time Suspension, Refusal, Cancellation, Scope Reduction and Expansion Policy Policy on the Use of Management Systems Certification Mark and Logo Service Process Flow Chart Application Form Management Systems Certification Contract Terms and Conditions with Client Complaint & Appeals Procedure Complaints Form Enquiry Training Training Services Training Services 2026 Training Calendar Ports & Border Port & Border: Field Inspection Process & Charges Port & Border Service Process Flow Chart Library Library Service Process Flow Chart Media Center News & Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng Translate", "content_hash": "f66cdd44e5822eb56009d8bf35669cfbfed1dfc47be934f54fb5efdbb0796d98", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:06.920379+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1865", "title": "2026 Appropriation Bill Details", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill-details", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill-details", "text": "2026 Appropriation Bill Details \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2026 Appropriation Bill Details Home 2026 Appropriation Bill Details 2026 Appropriation Bill Details Published on 8 January 2026 File Name: 2026 Appropriation Bill Details.pdf File Size: 7.46 MB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 11100 Hits Created Date: 01-08-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "4eab6bcb0d1d2d18be4e485662d23c416d5211e5f24f30e166c763dd1fac8ebd", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:08.054720+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1866", "title": "SON Elaborates Standards On Fortified Milled Rice", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/02/son-elaborates-standards-on-fortified-milled-rice/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/02/son-elaborates-standards-on-fortified-milled-rice/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) has hosted Stakeholders in the milled rice sector to a One-day Technical Committee meeting at the Lagos Sheraton Hotel, to deliberate on the draft of the Nigerian code of practice for processing and packaging of fortified milled rice. Addressing members of the Technical Committee, the Director General of SON, Mallam Farouk Salim, acknowledged the continued support of the TC Members in the elaboration of market-driven standards and also those with public health importance by way of providing technical know-how, expertise, and experience in standards elaboration processes. Mallam Salim, who was represented at the meeting by the Deputy Director and Head; of Foods and Codex Mr, Yunusa B. Mohammed, further appreciated the efforts of other Ministries and Agencies in creating a blueprint called the roadmap for scaling up rice fortification, which is aimed at reducing malnutrition in Nigeria. General overview of the Experts at the TC meeting He noted that addressing hunger and micronutrient deficiency remains a significant step towards promoting public health, accelerating national development, and achieving sustainable development in Nigeria. The SON helmsman reminded the Committee that micronutrient deficiency contributes to the high rate of Morbidity and Mortality in children and is a leading cause of Anemia in women amidst other related health issues. He, therefore, reiterated the importance of the code of practice as it would serve as a guideline and a recommendation to regulate the voluntary rice fortification regime in Nigeria and provide an opportunity for the industry to prepare for a mandatory rice fortification regime upon the elaboration of the Nigeria Industrial Standard for fortified milled rice. The DG thanked the Chairman of the Technical Committee Meeting, Dr. Adu Oluwatosin,a professor of Biochemistry at Lagos State University, and also Committee Members for their commitment to the assignment and implored them all to do their best and make decisions in the best interest of the Nation. Also speaking was the Chairman of the Working Group Committee, Professor Oluwatosin B Adu, who thanked the DG SON for the opportunity to chair this deliberation and implored the other stakeholders to put in their best on the assignment. The meeting had stakeholders from the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC), UN World Food Programme(WFP), Federal Competition & Consumer Protection Commission (FCCPC), and Institute of Public Analyst of Nigeria (IPAN), amongst others.", "content_hash": "5c05ed12070fe52925ea92f4b9939f2a59d6c9153bee8533c1b6dae73c053930", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:10.658925+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1867", "title": "2025 Repeal Bill", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-repeal-bill", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-repeal-bill", "text": "2025 Repeal Bill \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2025 Repeal Bill Home 2025 Repeal Bill 2025 Repeal Bill Published on 8 January 2026 File Name: 2025 Repeal Bill.pdf File Size: 217.85 KB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 2413 Hits Created Date: 01-08-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "67c5a050958afaa4c01d57c604d3fa4fdc32ce684cbd47502ccf06dfa5a1edb9", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:11.088554+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1868", "title": "EDER Deployment Son Pledges Continuous Synergy With Stakeholders", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/10/eder-deployment-son-pledges-continuous-synergy-with-stakeholders/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/10/eder-deployment-son-pledges-continuous-synergy-with-stakeholders/", "text": "It was an atmosphere of synergy, exchange of ideas, and collaboration as the Standards Organisation of Nigeria, under the leadership of the Director General and Chief Executive, Mallam Farouk Salim, continues to build on the success of emerging tops on the Ease of Doing Business ranking, to present Nigerians with its latest innovations, which is the Electronic Demand and Receipt concept to make transactions easier for stakeholders. In his welcome address, the DG stated that the electronic payment tools were conceived out of the desire to satisfy customers, as their importance cannot be over-emphasized. Mallam Farouk, represented by the Director of Finance and Accounts, Mr. Aaron Tam-George, said the sensitization program was organized to enlighten stakeholders on the Electronic payment tools, the Electronic Demand Note, and Electronic Receipts (EDER). Director Finance/Account Department, Aaron Tam-George giving the Director General\u2019s Welcome Address at the E- demand and E- receipt Sensitization in Port Harcourt In his words, \u201cThis Online payment scheme is designed to offer an end\u2013to\u2013end transactional experience for all our customers, business partners, and our internal organizational functions.\u201d He said the electronic mode of business payments and receipts, besides its convenience and safety, eliminates the hassles of cash logistics. \u201cThe essence of the E \u2013demand note and receipts is to promote the Federal Government\u2019s policy on \u201cEase of Doing Business\u201d where accountability and transparency is the watchword. Electronic Payment is very convenient for the consumer. It lowers transaction cost, increases government efficiency, boosts financial intermediation, and guarantees financial transparency.\u201d He said. Mallam Farouk further stated that \u201cthe use of the E \u2013 demand note and E- receipts holds the promise of broad benefits to our economy and stakeholders. He stated that SON was continually seeking ways to facilitate businesses by reducing or eliminating the bureaucracy associated with Public institutions.\u201d He posited, \u201cWe always remind ourselves that our stakeholders in the industrial sector are significant partners in our work. On this premise, we are here to educate our stakeholders on how this online payment and receiving technology will unarguably make business transactions easier.\u201d He charged the stakeholders to take advantage of the program to understand the Scheme and its implementation. Earlier on, the Director of SON South \u2013 South Directorate, Mr. Usman Mohammed, in his address, said that the event is one of the initiatives of the Organisation to bring together stakeholders from various sectors of the economy to discuss. These proffer solutions ensure they have value for their money through effective service delivery. The Director, South-South, while appreciating the DG and the SON Management for considering the value of the industries in the South\u2013South Region and sensitizing the stakeholders on the laudable initiative, he urged the stakeholders to take advantage of the occasion and be well informed so that they can enjoy the convenience of the online transaction platforms and bring it close to their businesses. L-R: Director of Public Relations Department, Mrs. Foluso Bolaji, Police Commissioner Rep, Customs Comptroller Rep, Head Importers, the Director, Finance/Account Department, Aaron Tam-George, the Head Importers, the Director South-South Region, U.S.Mohammed and the Director, Internal Audit, Mr. David Okon Also speaking at the event, the Chairman of Eastern Zone of the Presidential Monitoring Taskforce, Association of Nigeria Licensed Customs Agent, Chief Ndukwe Tobias, described the development as a mark of \u201cSON\u2019s consolidation on its improved openness and communication with stakeholders in recent times.\u201d Present at the event were Sister Agencies, Captains of industries, Importers, Independent Accredited Firms (IAFs), Manufacturers, and Clearing Agents. SON Officials at the event include; the Director of Internal Audit, Mr. David Okon; The Director of Public Relations, Mrs. Foluso Bolaji; The Regional Director South-South, U.S Mohammed; DD, Revenue and External Assistance, Mr. Adedayo David; Engr. Rose Madaki, Head, Onne Ports, and Borders; The Head, Inspection Compliance Department, Engr. Emmanuel Husseni, SON River State Coordinator, Engr. Lilian Gua; SON Staff, from Onne and Rivers State Officials.", "content_hash": "3dfb7ca34f1bab88916da44077613918fc89401d521d3ce890124cf1fb1fa5df", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:13.440200+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1869", "title": "2024 Repeal Bill", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2024-repeal-bill", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2024-repeal-bill", "text": "2024 Repeal Bill \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2024 Repeal Bill Home 2024 Repeal Bill 2024 Repeal Bill Published on 8 January 2026 File Name: 2024 Repeal Bill.pdf File Size: 266.9 KB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 2070 Hits Created Date: 01-08-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "acd1a645e3cfab750074c8c355ed6a7822eb62de0bff5efad920bdad240d9688", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:14.461038+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1870", "title": "SON To Collaborate With Pharmaceutical Association Of Nigerian Students (PANS) ABU, Zaria On Her Annual Symposium And Pansmanac Launch", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/17/son-to-collaborate-with-pharmaceutical-association-of-nigerian-students-pans-abu-zaria-on-her-annual-symposium-and-pansmanac-launch/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/08/17/son-to-collaborate-with-pharmaceutical-association-of-nigerian-students-pans-abu-zaria-on-her-annual-symposium-and-pansmanac-launch/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) in its usual collaborative move with MDA\u2019s, Institutions and Organizations alike felicitated with the Pharmaceutical Association of Nigerian Students of the Ahmadu Bello University (ABU) on the launch of the Association\u2019s Almanac. The Director General and Chief Executive, Mallam Farouk Salim an Alumnus of the University, who graduated from the Pharmacy Department was present as the Special Guest of Honour. Mallam Salim while addressing participants at the event acknowledged the WAZOBIA connection i.e. Prof Olobayo Kunle (Yoruba extraction), himself, Mallam Farouk Salim (Hausa) and Chief Emeka Duru of Igbo extraction all formed during their days back at ABU Zaria. Executive Members of The High Table He said that their relationship remained solid till this day and tasked the contemporary Pharmacists to desists from segregation that resorts to religious fanatism but rather the one that will bring solidarity and unity amongst them. The DG stated that any association built on the grounds of morals and psychological support will foster unity and create a friendly environment. The SON\u2019s helmsman stated that the Pharmaceutical sector can boast of trillions of Naira that would spur growth and contribute to the industry and economy of the Nation, especially in this period that the country\u2019s economy is recessed. He urged the Association to expand their horizons by identifying possible gaps in the department for immediate solutions rather than narrowing their obligations to studies alone. In his presentation titled \u201cAdvent of PharmD in Nigeria, The Fate of The Pharma Industries\u201d Prof Ahmed Tijjani Mora who was the Chairman of the Occasion acknowledged that the Council is challenged by the growing demand for Pharmacist to meet the growing population due to political upheaval, mismanagement of funds and climate change that have negative effect on humans, thus governed by rules and ethical codes that should at all times be strictly adhered to in other to raise the bar. Cross Section of Pharmaceutical Sciences Lecturers At The Front Row & PANS ABU Zaria Chapter He charged the Pharmacy department to be resilientt and portray a sense of patriotism given the utmost backing of the Vice Chancellor to the department. Also making a presentation was the Chief of Staff to the DG SON, Prof Olobayo Kunle with his paper titled, \u201cGrowth of Pharmacy Profession Through Participation in Politics\u201d, Prof. Kunle mentioned that pharmacists inter-phased with people daily putting the figure at an average of 25% in whatever location they serve. He maintained that a number of Pharmacists have expressed desires to become more involved in today\u2019s politics by becoming compensated for patient counselling as well as providing traditional medical services in advisory capacity. However, he affirmed that political advocacy has never been a major part of Pharmacists practice or viewed as necessary, but rather suggested to colleagues that even though they could become successful in politics but never to disconnect from the profession. Other presenters include; Pharmacist Ibrahim Baba Shehu Ahmed the Registrar, Pharmaceutical Council of Nigeria who made his presentation titled \u201cCurtailing drug markets saturated by non-professionals,\u201d and also Dr H. U. Ma\u2019aji HoD, Clinical & Practice Pharmacy) ABU Zaria, whose paper was titled \u201cThe Practice of Clinical Pharmacy in Community Pharmacy\u201d. The event ended with the launch of the PANS Almanac by DG SON and other invited Guests where the DG urged the Association to collaborate with SON by promoting the Organisation and its activities.", "content_hash": "c310d8db461c0da39919786f5623c341638d43349d66c22f5f997377b38868dd", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:16.688252+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1871", "title": "2026 Appropriation Bill", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill", "text": "2026 Appropriation Bill \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2026 Appropriation Bill Home 2026 Appropriation Bill 2026 Appropriation Bill Published on 8 January 2026 File Name: 2026 Appropriation Bill.pdf File Size: 282.79 KB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 22499 Hits Created Date: 01-08-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Audit